---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'About DroidDiagnostics';
const description = 'DroidDiagnostics is a privacy-first Android and AOSP diagnostic triage tool that analyzes supported logs locally in the browser.';
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <section class="content-page"><div class="shell"><header class="content-header"><span class="kicker">About</span><h1>Diagnostics should start with evidence.</h1><p>DroidDiagnostics is built to turn large Android diagnostic archives into a smaller set of reviewable findings without sending the source archive to a server.</p></header><section class="card prose-card"><h2>MVP scope</h2><p>The current engine focuses on reboot, ANR, Java/native crash, kernel, biometric, display, thermal, and boot failure signatures. It is a triage tool: it helps engineers find relevant evidence faster, but it does not claim that a matched line alone proves root cause.</p></section><section class="card prose-card"><h2>Designed to expand</h2><p>The analyzer uses independent subsystem modules and a common finding model so tombstone symbolization, dedicated logcat analysis, APK inspection, vendor-specific rules, and optional explanation layers can be added without replacing the core pipeline.</p></section></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
